# __NS__-loop

Run `./scripts/__NS__-tick.sh` from the `__NS__` loop's infra worktree root
(`../<repo>-harness-ns-__NS__`) and report what it did.

That is the entire skill. The intelligence is in the scripts — this exists only so
`/loop` has a slash-command-shaped target. Do not do any feature work in this
session; the scripts shell out to fresh `claude -p` subprocesses for all real work,
which is what keeps this outer session's context from bloating across ticks.

`__NS__-tick.sh` first force-syncs the infra worktree to a clean `origin/main` (so
`__NS__-dispatch.sh`, its shared `harness-lib.sh`, and `.harness/env` are always
current), then `exec`s `./scripts/__NS__-dispatch.sh` — the deterministic,
HEAD-agnostic dispatcher. Never point `/loop` at the dispatcher directly, or
loop-infrastructure updates merged to main won't reach the loop.

This loop is independent of the build loop (`/poll-and-dispatch`) and the memory
loop (`/learn-loop`); the three never block each other and coordinate only through
git. Start it in its own session:

```
cd ../<repo>-harness-ns-__NS__
claude
/loop 5m /__NS__-loop
```
